<title>USA: Marathon raises US posted crude oil prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon raises US posted crude oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Thursday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $16.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $15.90 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $16.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $16.75.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
